Feature: F6 rt_behavior — the runtime-operand law over fold-opaque argv operands (folded from the retired rt_behavior.tkr, dir removido) (unfolded from regressor.tkr — members of this project's single build)

  # One program, compiled ONCE; every row RUNS the built binary with argv operands that
  # arrive through the process boundary, so the compiler cannot const-fold the op under
  # test — the emitted native code must perform it at run time. Oracles: exit + stdout.

  Scenario Outline: <op> of fold-opaque operands yields <out> (exit <r>)
    Given args = ["<op>", "<a>", "<b>"]
    Given env = ["TEKO_REGR_ENTRY=q183_op_of_fold_opaque_operands_yields_out"]
    When built and run
    Then exit = <r>
    And stdout = "<out>"
    Examples:
      | op      | a   | b   | r   | out    |
      | add     | 12  | 10  | 22  | 22     |
      | sub     | 30  | 8   | 22  | 22     |
      | mul     | 6   | 7   | 42  | 42     |
      | div     | 84  | 2   | 42  | 42     |
      | mod     | 100 | 29  | 13  | 13     |
      | band    | 12  | 10  | 8   | 8      |
      | bor     | 12  | 10  | 14  | 14     |
      | bxor    | 12  | 10  | 6   | 6      |
      | shl     | 1   | 65  | 2   | 2      |
      | shr     | 255 | 1   | 127 | 127    |
      | lt      | 3   | 5   | 1   | 1      |
      | eq      | 7   | 7   | 1   | 1      |
      | concat  | foo | bar | 6   | foobar |
      | foreach | 5   | 0   | 15  | 15     |
      | idxset  | 2   | 9   | 9   | 9      |


Feature: F9 romaneio .31 — the audit's positive regressions (backend x scenario) (unfolded from regressor.tkr — members of this project's single build)

  # (B-S1) The own backend coerces into a null-union at EVERY placement that declares a type, not
  # only at the binding: `x = null` after a `T | null` binding used to write a raw `const 0` into the
  # VReg the `match` then reads as the wrapper's base address — a load from address 0. The `c` rows
  # are the differential control: the C backend wrapped at the assign all along.

  Scenario: ref_forwarding_same_referent_compiles
    Given env = ["TEKO_REGR_ENTRY=q187_ref_forwarding_same_referent_compiles"]
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42

  # (Block 12) The scenario binary runs with its CWD in its OWN scratch, not in the repository root.
  # The probe writes a RELATIVE file (which must therefore land in the scratch, not the work tree)
  # and then proves where it is by looking for a file that exists ONLY at the repo root.


