Feature: qualified_optional members — KNOWN-STOP pins for the cells held back from the two restored regressives

  # A construct the restored `np_oop` fixture above WANTED and could not have, pinned rather than
  # dropped so that the day the stop lifts the pin fails LOUDLY and forces the direct spelling back
  # into `src/np_oop/entry.tks`. It is a CODEGEN-stage stop, so unlike the parse- and checker-stage
  # folds in the two compile-fail projects it cannot share a failing build with anything: a build
  # that reaches codegen is one whose checker PASSED. One build, and it is the only one this project
  # pays beyond its own.
  #
  # The two #265 `[](T | null)` cells are pinned ONCE, not twice: the parser refuses to spell the
  # type at all, which is the first wall and the one that has to fall first, and that pin folds into
  # examples/regressions/parse_diagnostics at zero build cost
  # (`src/pin_slice_opt_param`). A second pin behind it would cost a build to assert a `cc` failure
  # message that is not the compiler's own diagnostic.
  Scenario: KNOWN-STOP — a bare-null match arm into a `T | null` slot (np_oop held-back spelling)
    Given source = "cases/bare_null_match_arm_optional.tks"
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "nested bare-null optional"

